// A table of nothing but providers: every row is well-formed on its own, and
// between them they leave the game with no house at all. `Inconsistency::NoHouse`
// is the only thing wrong with it.
//
// **Why this is a file and not a one-word replacement.** Until phase 14.4 it
// was one: emptying the house's `required_services` was enough, because that
// was how a house was recognised. A row now declares its role, so producing a
// house-less table takes a row that is a *valid provider* instead — which is
// the check becoming harder to trip by accident, and the reason it is worth
// keeping rather than a reason to delete it. The house levels in `rules.ron`
// still describe three levels of a house nobody builds, and that is exactly
// the silence `NoHouse` exists to break.
(
    buildings: [
        (
            id: "well",
            size: (1, 1),
            cost: 12,
            levels: 1,
            role: "provider",
            service: Some((kind: "water", range_per_level: [12], capacity_per_level: [32])),
        ),
        (
            id: "farm",
            size: (2, 2),
            cost: 40,
            levels: 1,
            role: "provider",
            service: Some((kind: "food", range_per_level: [10], capacity_per_level: [20])),
            output_per_tick: Some(400),
            max_stock: Some(20000),
        ),
    ],
)
